    "durationMs": 124678,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Implementation** — FastAPI 0.115.5 + SQLAlchemy 2.0 + psycopg 3, with Alembic migrations:\n- `app/` — config (reads `DATABASE_URL` from env, no hard-coded credentials), models, Pydantic schemas, CRUD, and routes\n- `migrations/` — autogenerated migration creating the `links` table (unique indexed code, url, clicks, created_at)\n- `start.sh` — runs `alembic upgrade head` then serves uvicorn on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground\n- `README.md` — startup instructions; `requirements.txt` — pinned deps; `tests/` — 12-test pytest suite\n\n**Verified over real HTTP against `sh start.sh`:**\n- POST creates links (201, clicks 0), returns submitted URL unchanged, generates unique 8-char codes, 409 with `error` on duplicate codes\n- GET /links/{code} returns the link or 404 with `error`; GET /r/{code} returns 302 with correct `Location` and increments clicks exactly once\n- GET /links lists in ascending creation order with `items`/`total`\n- 422 with `error` for malformed JSON, missing/invalid url (non-absolute, non-http(s), no host), and invalid codes (also invalid codes in path params)\n- Persistence: killed and restarted the server — links and click counts survived\n\nThe database is left clean (empty table, schema at migration head), so the test suite starts fresh."
  }
